---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const pageTitle = "Flooring & Subfloor Options | Appalachian Sheds Inc.";
const pageDescription = "Compare structural floor systems, 2\u00d76 pressure-treated tongue-and-groove upgrades, and popular flooring finishes for premium backyard sheds.";
---
<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
<Fragment set:html={"<section class=\"article-hero\"><div class=\"shell\"><div class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/options-upgrades/\">Options &amp; Upgrades</a> / Flooring &amp; Subfloor Options</div><div class=\"eyebrow\">APPALACHIAN SHEDS INC. \u00b7 OPTIONS &amp; UPGRADES</div><h1>Flooring &amp; Subfloor Options</h1><p>Structural floor systems, premium tongue-and-groove upgrades, practical finishes, and flooring decisions based on use.</p></div></section><section aria-label=\"Flooring planning price information\" class=\"asi-floor-integrity-note\"><div class=\"shell\"><p><strong>Flooring price guidance:</strong> Prices and material costs shown below are preserved from the original 2026 planning source and are not verified current ASI selling prices. Any upgrade, substrate suitability, structural load rating, product availability, and final installed price are confirmed in the written proposal.</p></div></section><section aria-labelledby=\"asi-floor-final-title\" id=\"asi-floor-final\">\n<div class=\"aff-shell\">\n<header class=\"aff-head\">\n<p class=\"aff-kicker\">Options &amp; Upgrades \u00b7 Flooring &amp; Structural Floor Systems</p>\n<h2 class=\"aff-title\" id=\"asi-floor-final-title\">Choose the Floor for the Weight, Moisture and Daily Use the Building Will Actually See</h2>\n<p class=\"aff-subtitle\">Structural Subfloors \u00b7 2\u00d76 T&amp;G Upgrade \u00b7 Workshop Floors \u00b7 Finished Floors \u00b7 Protective Surfaces</p>\n<p class=\"aff-lede\">The floor is both structure and finish. A mower shed needs a different surface from an office. A workshop may need impact and chemical resistance. A premium studio may need a smooth, residential-looking finish. Appalachian Sheds separates the structural floor from the finish flooring so the customer understands what carries the load and what creates the final surface.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"aff-divider\"></div>\n</header>\n<nav aria-label=\"Flooring options navigation\" class=\"aff-nav\">\n<a href=\"#asi-floor-structural\"><strong>Structural Floor Systems</strong><span>Standard + Premium</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-floor-tg\"><strong>2\u00d76 T&amp;G Upgrade Pricing</strong><span>Most Requested Upgrade</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-floor-top10\"><strong>Top 10 Flooring Options</strong><span>National Builder Comparison</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-floor-use\"><strong>Best Floor by Use</strong><span>Storage \u00b7 Workshop \u00b7 Office</span></a>\n</nav>\n<section class=\"aff-direct\">\n<span>Direct Answer</span>\n<h3>The Most-Requested Structural Floor Upgrade Is 2\u00d76 Pressure-Treated Tongue-and-Groove Southern Yellow Pine.</h3>\n<p>Compared with a conventional \u00be-inch plywood or premium engineered-panel floor, the 2\u00d76 T&amp;G system provides a substantially thicker solid-wood deck, excellent stiffness, a traditional heavy-duty appearance and a floor that feels more substantial under equipment and foot traffic. It is priced as an upgrade above the standard floor already included in the building\u2014not as a second full floor charge.</p>\n</section>\n<!-- STRUCTURAL SYSTEMS -->\n<section class=\"aff-section\" id=\"asi-floor-structural\">\n<div class=\"aff-section-head\">\n<div class=\"aff-section-copy\">\n<span class=\"aff-mini\">Structural Floor Systems</span>\n<h3>Start With the Structural Deck Before Choosing the Finish Surface</h3>\n<p>National shed builders commonly use treated plywood or engineered tongue-and-groove panels as their primary structural floor decking. Old Hickory, for example, offers both treated plywood and engineered tongue-and-groove floor systems with thicker upgrades available for increased capacity.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-section-side\">\n<span class=\"aff-mini\">ASI Premium Upgrade</span>\n<h3>2\u00d76 T&amp;G Pressure-Treated Solid Wood</h3>\n<p>For customers who want a more substantial structural deck than a \u00be-inch panel floor, ASI can upgrade to pressure-treated 2\u00d76 tongue-and-groove Southern Yellow Pine.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-tablebox\">\n<div class=\"aff-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"aff-table\">\n<thead><tr><th>Structural Floor</th><th>Typical Material</th><th>Thickness</th><th>Best Use</th><th>2026 Installed Planning Range</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>\u00be\" Pressure-Treated Plywood</td><td>Ground-contact treated plywood</td><td>23/32\" nominal</td><td>General storage, mower and workshop use</td><td>$2.75\u2013$4.25 / SF</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Premium Engineered OSB</td><td>AdvanTech / comparable premium T&amp;G engineered panel</td><td>23/32\" nominal</td><td>Flat, stiff, moisture-resistant panel floor</td><td>$3.00\u2013$4.75 / SF</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Standard OSB</td><td>Commodity T&amp;G OSB subfloor panel</td><td>23/32\" nominal</td><td>Budget applications only</td><td>$1.75\u2013$3.00 / SF</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2\u00d76 PT Tongue-and-Groove</td><td>Pressure-treated Southern Yellow Pine</td><td>1\u00bd\" actual</td><td>Premium structural floor, equipment and heavy-use feel</td><td>Priced as size-based upgrade below</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- 2X6 T&G -->\n<section class=\"aff-section\" id=\"asi-floor-tg\">\n<div class=\"aff-section-head\">\n<div class=\"aff-section-copy\">\n<span class=\"aff-mini\">Most-Requested Premium Subfloor Upgrade</span>\n<h3>2\u00d76 Pressure-Treated Tongue-and-Groove Structural Floor</h3>\n<p>Current Ohio retail pricing for pressure-treated 2\u00d76\u00d716 T&amp;G Southern Yellow Pine is roughly $23.89\u2013$26.53 per board. Each board has an actual face width of approximately 5\u00bd inches, so this floor uses substantially more wood volume than a panel floor and requires individual-board fitting, fastening and alignment.</p>\n<p>The upgrade table below includes premium T&amp;G material, additional installation labor, overhead / warranty / margin allowance and a credit for the standard floor that the premium floor replaces.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-section-side\">\n<span class=\"aff-mini\">Important Pricing Method</span>\n<h3>The Customer Is Not Charged Twice for the Floor.</h3>\n<p>The standard \u00be-inch floor allowance is credited back before the final T&amp;G upgrade price is established.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-two\">\n<section class=\"aff-panel\">\n<h4>Why Customers Choose It</h4>\n<ul class=\"aff-list\">\n<li>Approximately twice the thickness of a \u00be-inch panel floor</li>\n<li>Solid pressure-treated Southern Yellow Pine</li>\n<li>Tongue-and-groove edges create a continuous interlocked deck</li>\n<li>Substantial feel under mowers, equipment and workshop use</li>\n<li>Attractive traditional plank appearance when left exposed</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"aff-panel\">\n<h4>Installation Direction</h4>\n<ul class=\"aff-list\">\n<li>Boards installed perpendicular to supporting floor framing</li>\n<li>T&amp;G joints fitted tightly without damaging tongue profile</li>\n<li>Exterior-rated structural fasteners used at framing</li>\n<li>Board ends supported / framed as required by layout</li>\n<li>Field cuts treated where required by preservative manufacturer's instructions</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-tablebox\">\n<div class=\"aff-table-head\">\n<h4>2026 ASI 2\u00d76 PT T&amp;G Upgrade Pricing \u2014 Material, Labor &amp; Overhead Included</h4>\n<p>Planning model uses current Ohio T&amp;G material costs, fasteners / waste, added board-by-board labor, overhead / warranty / margin and a credit for the standard \u00be-inch structural floor being replaced.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"aff-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Building Size</th>\n<th>Floor Area</th>\n<th>Premium T&amp;G Material</th>\n<th>Added Labor</th>\n<th>Overhead / Warranty / Margin</th>\n<th>Standard Floor Credit</th>\n<th>Calculated Upgrade</th>\n<th>ASI Planning Upgrade Price</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>8\u00d78</td><td>64 SF</td><td>$266</td><td>$112</td><td>$86</td><td>\u2212$160</td><td>$304</td><td><strong>$375</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>8\u00d710</td><td>80 SF</td><td>$332</td><td>$140</td><td>$108</td><td>\u2212$200</td><td>$380</td><td><strong>$400</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>10\u00d712</td><td>120 SF</td><td>$498</td><td>$210</td><td>$162</td><td>\u2212$300</td><td>$570</td><td><strong>$575</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>12\u00d714</td><td>168 SF</td><td>$697</td><td>$294</td><td>$227</td><td>\u2212$420</td><td>$798</td><td><strong>$800</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>12\u00d716</td><td>192 SF</td><td>$797</td><td>$336</td><td>$259</td><td>\u2212$480</td><td>$912</td><td><strong>$925</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>14\u00d716</td><td>224 SF</td><td>$930</td><td>$392</td><td>$302</td><td>\u2212$560</td><td>$1,064</td><td><strong>$1,075</strong></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"aff-note\">These are 2026 planning prices, not permanent fixed prices. T&amp;G lumber availability, treatment, grade and freight can materially affect the final written option price. The standard-floor credit assumes the T&amp;G upgrade is selected before the standard deck is installed.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- TOP 10 -->\n<section class=\"aff-section\" id=\"asi-floor-top10\">\n<div class=\"aff-section-head\">\n<div class=\"aff-section-copy\">\n<span class=\"aff-mini\">National Shed-Builder Flooring Comparison</span>\n<h3>Top 10 Shed Flooring Options \u2014 Features, Use &amp; Cincinnati Tri-State Planning Costs</h3>\n<p>The list below combines common national shed-builder structural floor choices with the finish surfaces most often used in workshops, garages, hobby sheds, offices and studios.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-section-side\">\n<span class=\"aff-mini\">Important</span>\n<h3>Structural Deck and Finish Flooring Are Different Layers.</h3>\n<p>LVP, rubber, PVC tiles and LuxGuard normally install over an existing plywood or engineered structural floor. They do not replace the framing or structural subfloor unless specifically designed to do so.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-cards\">\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">01</span>\n<h4>\u00be\" Pressure-Treated Plywood</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is popular:</strong> strong, familiar, rot-resistant and practical for storage and mower buildings.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> panels laid over joists, seams staggered where layout permits, glued / fastened per assembly requirements.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> $2.75\u2013$4.25/SF installed.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">02</span>\n<h4>Premium Engineered T&amp;G OSB \u2014 AdvanTech / Comparable</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is popular:</strong> high stiffness, consistent panel quality and improved moisture resistance versus commodity OSB.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> T&amp;G panels installed over floor framing with manufacturer-approved fastening.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> $3.00\u2013$4.75/SF installed.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">03</span>\n<h4>Standard T&amp;G OSB \u2014 Budget Structural Floor</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is used:</strong> lowest-cost structural panel option.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> panel floor over joists; exposed edges and repeated wetting should be avoided.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> $1.75\u2013$3.00/SF installed.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">04</span>\n<h4>Concrete Slab</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is used:</strong> permanent, rot-proof and well suited to garages and heavy equipment.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> excavation, compacted base, forms, reinforcement, concrete placement, finishing and curing.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> approximately $7\u2013$12+/SF for straightforward small slabs; site prep can add materially.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">05</span>\n<h4>Rubber Mats / Interlocking Rubber Tiles</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is used:</strong> impact absorption, traction, comfort underfoot and easy replacement.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> installed over a flat structural floor; loose-lay or interlocking depending system.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> $4\u2013$9+/SF installed depending thickness and product.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">06</span>\n<h4>Luxury Vinyl Plank \u2014 LVP</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is used:</strong> residential appearance, easy cleaning and broad style choice for offices and studios.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> installed over a smooth, flat structural subfloor; manufacturer temperature limits must be respected.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> $4\u2013$8/SF for small detached-building installations.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">07</span>\n<h4>Epoxy / Polyaspartic Coating \u2014 Concrete Only</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is used:</strong> chemical resistance, easy cleaning and premium workshop / garage appearance.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> concrete mechanically prepared, repaired as required, then coated with compatible primer / base / topcoat system.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> roughly $6\u2013$8.50/SF for typical epoxy-flake work; premium systems can run higher.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">08</span>\n<h4>Interlocking PVC Garage Tiles</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is used:</strong> durable modular workshop surface that can be replaced in sections.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> tiles snap together over a clean, flat plywood or concrete floor.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> $5\u2013$9+/SF installed.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">09</span>\n<h4>Sheet Vinyl</h4>\n<p><strong>Why it is used:</strong> economical finished appearance with fewer seams than plank systems.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> smooth underlayment required; sheet is fit, bonded / perimeter-secured according to product requirements and trimmed at edges.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 Cincinnati planning:</strong> $3.50\u2013$6.50/SF on small projects.</p>\n</article>\n<article class=\"aff-card\">\n<span class=\"aff-num\">10</span>\n<h4>LuxGuard\u00ae Premium Rollout Rubber Flooring</h4>\n<p><strong>What it actually is:</strong> textured, impermeable rubber flooring with fiberglass backing developed specifically for sheds, garages and industrial-style use.</p>\n<p><strong>Application:</strong> rolled over the wood subfloor and mechanically secured / adhered according to the manufacturer's installation method.</p>\n<p><strong>2026 planning:</strong> national shed dealers currently advertise roughly $3.10\u2013$4.00/SF as an upgrade; ASI should plan approximately $4\u2013$6/SF installed until supplier freight and dealer pricing are confirmed.</p>\n</article>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- USE CASE -->\n<section class=\"aff-compare\" id=\"asi-floor-use\">\n<div class=\"aff-compare-head\">\n<h3>Choose the Flooring by Building Use</h3>\n<p>The floor should match the moisture, weight, traffic and appearance requirements of the building.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"aff-table\">\n<thead><tr><th>Building Use</th><th>Recommended Structural Floor</th><th>Recommended Finish Surface</th><th>Main Priority</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>General Storage</td><td>\u00be\" PT plywood or premium engineered panel</td><td>Leave exposed or apply protective finish</td><td>Durability and value</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Mower / Equipment Shed</td><td>\u00be\" PT plywood or 2\u00d76 PT T&amp;G</td><td>LuxGuard\u00ae, rubber or durable exposed structural deck</td><td>Wheel loads, water, mud and traction</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Workshop</td><td>2\u00d76 PT T&amp;G or premium engineered panel</td><td>LuxGuard\u00ae, PVC tile, rubber or coated surface</td><td>Impact, chemicals and cleanability</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Backyard Office</td><td>Premium engineered panel or smooth plywood</td><td>LVP or engineered wood</td><td>Appearance, comfort and cleanability</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Creative Studio</td><td>Premium engineered panel</td><td>LVP, rubber or engineered wood</td><td>Comfort, acoustics and appearance</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pool House</td><td>Moisture-tolerant structural deck</td><td>LuxGuard\u00ae, rubber, PVC or compatible resilient flooring</td><td>Wet traffic and slip resistance</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Garage / Heavy Equipment</td><td>Concrete slab or engineered heavy-duty wood floor</td><td>Epoxy / polyaspartic on concrete or heavy-duty rubber</td><td>Load, oils, abrasion and permanence</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"aff-cta\">\n<div class=\"aff-cta-copy\">\n<h3>Start With the Structural Floor \u2014 Then Choose the Surface</h3>\n<p>Appalachian Sheds can match the floor system to mower loads, workshop use, wet traffic, finished-office expectations and future flooring so the customer understands both the structure underfoot and the surface they will actually see.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"aff-cta-side\">\n<a href=\"/options-upgrades/\">Explore Options &amp; Upgrades</a>\n<a class=\"aff-ghost\" href=\"tel:15133792421\">Call Edwin \u00b7 (513) 379-2421</a>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</section>"} />
</Base>

